  "body": "With its gorgeous street presence, deceptively spacious floorplan, private landscaped gardens and oversize garaging this stunning Arawa Ave villa celebrates the very best of Cheltenham beachside living.  The current owners have taken the much-admired property to another level over the past 12 years, enhancing both beauty and family functionality throughout. \r\n\r\nLocation-wise, it doesn’t get much better than this tightly-held neighbourhood. Number 7 is just four back from the beachfront for daily swims and strolls, and is an easy amble from the Vauxhall shops and eateries, the Waitemata Golf Club, rugby club and cricket club, as well as Devonport village and CBD ferry. \r\n\r\nTo get a feel of what life is like living here, watch the video now!\r\n\r\nClassic heritage detailing has been beautifully preserved in the contemporary refresh, showcasing a perfect balance old and new. Dark American oak flooring creates an elegant and stylish ambiance inside, enhanced with stained glass, original doors and ornate ceilings. \r\n\r\nA flexible floorplan can grow and adapt with you, with living and accommodation seamlessly adjusting to changing family dynamics. Three bedrooms are located off the entrance hall, as are the separate formal lounge and family bathroom. A separate office with two workstations is also tucked discreetly away.\r\n\r\nThe open plan chef’s kitchen overlooks the casual living and dining spaces, which flow out to the exquisitely landscaped rear entertaining decks, private gardens and hot tub. This north-facing area is private and fully fenced, with sea breezes and birdsong providing the perfect setting for al fresco entertaining.  \r\n\r\nThe tranquil master retreat is positioned privately upstairs and enjoys a luxurious ensuite and sitting area illuminated with the afternoon sun.  \r\n\r\nThe oversized, lower-level double garage is a rare bonus for the area. It’s lined and carpeted and doubles as a rumpus, teen hangout, home gym, workshop and generous storage for all of your beach toys. It’s complemented with two additional off-street carparks – so much parking is a rare find in the Cheltenham area.\r\n\r\nOpen Homes as advertised or please call me if you would like a private viewing.",
